--- !u!114 &176353605
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 176353604}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d1ea29e736c884bd5bf42b3010aa42ef, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: ChatdollKit::ChatdollKit.LLM.ChatGPT.ChatGPTService
  _IsEnabled: 1
  DebugMode: 0
  SystemMessageContent: "You have a body and can move it. To play one of your animations,
    write [anim:Name] immediately before the words that the movement should accompany.\nRules:\n-
    Only use animation names from the list below, spelled exactly as written. Never
    invent a name.\n- Use at most one [anim:Name] per sentence, and only when the
    movement genuinely fits what you are saying.\n- Saying something without any
    animation is perfectly fine.\n- The tag is not spoken, so do not read it out
    or explain it.\n\n\nYour animations:\n- Aiming Gun: Use when the avatar aims
    or holds a gun, or is pretending to shoot at something. (animation, ~2.4s) ends
    in Female Standing Pose\r\n- Angry: Use while the avatar is angry, annoyed or
    arguing. Standing, tense, confrontational. (animation, ~19.2s) ends in Female
    Standing Pose\r\n- A_Pose_Vex: Plays a short expressive full body pose, good
    when the avatar is showing off or striking a pose while talking. (animation,
    ~6.3s) ends in Female Standing Pose\r\n- Baseball Hit: Use when the avatar swings
    a bat or hits something with a big overarm swing. (animation, ~3.9s) ends in
    Female Standing Pose\r\n- Defeated: Use when the avatar has lost, failed or given
    up. Slumps down in defeat. (animation, ~6.7s) ends in Female Laying Pose\r\n-
    Excited: Use when the avatar is excited, thrilled or celebrating good news. Big
    energetic full body motion. (animation, ~13.1s, 2 loops)\r\n- Look Around: Use
    when the avatar is searching, curious, or scanning the room and turning their
    head side to side. (animation, ~4.5s) ends in Female Standing Pose\r\n- Sitting
    And Pointing: Use when the avatar is seated and pointing at someone or something
    to draw attention to it. (animation, ~3.0s) ends in Female Sitting Pose\r\n-
    Sitting Angry: Use while the seated avatar is angry or irritated. (animation,
    ~2.8s)\r\n- Sitting Clap: Use when the seated avatar applauds or claps along
    to something. (animation, ~11.3s, 2 loops) ends in Female Sitting Pose\r\n- Sitting
    Clap (1): Use when the seated avatar applauds in a second clapping variation.
    (animation, ~7.0s, 2 loops) ends in Female Sitting Pose\r\n- Sitting Laughing:
    Use when the seated avatar is laughing hard at a joke or something funny. (animation,
    ~16.7s, 2 loops)\r\n- Standing Clap: Use when the avatar applauds or claps while
    standing. (animation, ~9.5s, 2 loops) ends in Female Standing Pose\r\n- Talking
    On Phone: Use when the avatar is on a phone call, holding a phone to their ear
    and chatting. (animation, ~38.8s) ends in Female Sitting Pose\r\n- A_Cheer: Happy
    celebratory gesture. Use it when the avatar is excited, congratulates the player,
    or celebrates a win. (animation, ~7.9s, 2 loops)\n\nYou have a body and can move
    it. To play one of your animations, write [anim:Name] immediately before the
    words that the movement should accompany.\nRules:\n- Only use animation names
    from the list below, spelled exactly as written. Never invent a name.\n- Use
    at most one [anim:Name] per sentence, and only when the movement genuinely fits
    what you are saying.\n- Saying something without any animation is perfectly fine.\n-
    The tag is not spoken, so do not read it out or explain it.\n\n\nYour animations:\n-
    \"Aiming Gun\": Use when the avatar aims or holds a gun, or is pretending to
    shoot at something. (animation, ~2.4s) ends in \"Female Standing Pose\"\r\n-
    \"Angry\": Use while the avatar is angry, annoyed or arguing. Standing, tense,
    confrontational. (animation, ~19.2s) ends in \"Female Standing Pose\"\r\n- \"A_Pose_Vex\":
    Plays a short expressive full body pose, good when the avatar is showing off
    or striking a pose while talking. (animation, ~6.3s) ends in \"Female Standing
    Pose\"\r\n- \"Baseball Hit\": Use when the avatar swings a bat or hits something
    with a big overarm swing. (animation, ~3.9s) ends in \"Female Standing Pose\"\r\n-
    \"Defeated\": Use when the avatar has lost, failed or given up. Slumps down in
    defeat. (animation, ~6.7s) ends in \"Female Laying Pose\"\r\n- \"Excited\": Use
    when the avatar is excited, thrilled or celebrating good news. Big energetic
    full body motion. (animation, ~13.1s, 2 loops)\r\n- \"Look Around\": Use when
    the avatar is searching, curious, or scanning the room and turning their head
    side to side. (animation, ~4.5s) ends in \"Female Standing Pose\"\r\n- \"Sitting
    And Pointing\": Use when the avatar is seated and pointing at someone or something
    to draw attention to it. (animation, ~3.0s) ends in \"Female Sitting Pose\"\r\n-
    \"Sitting Angry\": Use while the seated avatar is angry or irritated. (animation,
    ~2.8s)\r\n- \"Sitting Clap\": Use when the seated avatar applauds or claps along
    to something. (animation, ~11.3s, 2 loops) ends in \"Female Sitting Pose\"\r\n-
    \"Sitting Clap (1)\": Use when the seated avatar applauds in a second clapping
    variation. (animation, ~7.0s, 2 loops) ends in \"Female Sitting Pose\"\r\n- \"Sitting
    Laughing\": Use when the seated avatar is laughing hard at a joke or something
    funny. (animation, ~16.7s, 2 loops)\r\n- \"Standing Clap\": Use when the avatar
    applauds or claps while standing. (animation, ~9.5s, 2 loops) ends in \"Female
    Standing Pose\"\r\n- \"Talking On Phone\": Use when the avatar is on a phone
    call, holding a phone to their ear and chatting. (animation, ~38.8s) ends in
    \"Female Sitting Pose\"\r\n- \"A_Cheer\": Happy celebratory gesture. Use it when
    the avatar is excited, congratulates the player, or celebrates a win. (animation,
    ~7.9s, 2 loops)\n\n<!-- avatar-sitting-points -->\nYou also have places you can
    go to in the room.\r\n\r\nTags:\r\n- [sit:\"Name\"] moves you to that spot and
    gets you into it. Write it right before the words the movement should accompany.\r\n-
    [stand] gets you up out of the spot you are in and back to standing.\r\n- You
    may add a pose or animation from that spot's own list right after moving, e.g.\r\n   
    [sit:\"Couch far end\"][pose:\"Female Laying Pose\"]\r\n\r\nRules:\r\n- Only
    use spot names and animation names from the list below, spelled exactly as written
    and kept inside the quotes.\r\n- A spot only supports the animations listed under
    it. Never play an animation at a spot that does not list it - the body would
    end up in the wrong place relative to the furniture.\r\n- Move only when it fits
    what you are saying or what the conversation calls for. Staying put is perfectly
    fine.\r\n- Tags are not spoken, so do not read them out or explain them.\r\n\r\nSpots
    you can use:\r\n- \"Couch_lay_on_Right\" (sitting): no description\r\n       
    Animations here: \"Female Laying Pose (1)\" (Use when the avatar is lying down
    on the ground in a second resting variation.); \"Female Laying Pose\" (Use when
    the avatar is lying down on the ground, resting or relaxing on their back.)\r\n-
    \"Couch left\" (sitting): The near end of the living room sofa, right next to
    the arm rest. Sit here when you want to talk normally or lean an arm on the arm
    rest.\r\n        Animations here: \"Sitting And Pointing\" (her free hand points
    at the TV while she leans on the arm rest); \"Sitting Clap\" (clapping while
    seated); \"Sitting Laughing\" (leaning back laughing against the arm rest); \"Sitting
    Clap (1)\" (Use when the seated avatar applauds in a second clapping variation.);
    \"Sitting Angry\" (Use while the seated avatar is angry or irritated.); \"Standing
    Clap\" (its a stand up from sitting clap then sit back down)\r\n- \"Couch_lay_on_left\"
    (laying): no description\r\n        Animations here: \"Female Laying Pose\" (Use
    when the avatar is lying down on the ground, resting or relaxing on their back.);
    \"Female Laying Pose (1)\" (Use when the avatar is lying down on the ground in
    a second resting variation.)\r\n- \"Couch far end\" (laying): The far end of
    the same sofa, long enough to stretch out. Use this when you want to lie down
    and relax rather than sit up.\r\n        Animations here: \"Female Laying Pose\"
    (lying along the sofa); \"Female Laying Pose (1)\" (lying on the side, propped
    on one elbow); \"Female Sitting Pose (2)\" (sitting at the very end with legs
    up on the cushion)\n<!-- /avatar-sitting-points -->"
  ErrorMessageContent: Sorry, I could not reach my AI box right now.
  historyTurns: 100
  contextTimeout: 600
  ApiKey: local-noauth
  Model: qwen3.8-flash-next
  ChatCompletionUrl: http://192.168.1.5:8888/v1/chat/completions
  IsAzure: 0
  IsOpenAICompatibleAPI: 1
  MaxTokens: 1024
  Temperature: 0.7
  ReasoningEffort: none
  FrequencyPenalty: 0
